at last you've got your grabby robot  hands on the long-awaited titanfall and  you're ready to run on some walls shoot  some faces and kick some butts though  you start off with some decent weaponry  things only get better as you diversify  your loadout options so here are some  tips to help you level up quickly and  get those unlocks start off by playing  campaign multiplayer the action is  pretty much the same as the standard  action in classic multiplayer but by  completing each side of the campaign  you'll unlock the ogre and Strider  chassis z' for use in your custom Titan  loadouts you can always use each chassis  and a preset loadout of course but you  want to be able to build your own beast  almost every match starts with the  running of the grunts AI soldier's flood  the field of battle and pilots swarm to  feed on the easy prey grunt inspector  kills earn you attrition points and  speed up your Titan build but they're  also tied to a lot of weapon attachment  unlocks like scopes and suppressors and  extended magazines and such check the  challenges for each bit of gear you want  to unlock and then focus on the  appropriate prey if you have the right  burn card select an amped version of the  weapon that you want to earn unlocks for  because it'll help you kill your quarry  more efficiently and it'll totally count  towards your unlock progress if however  you're just looking to farm grunts for  straight XP choose the preset assassin  class and rock the suppressed smart  pistol that thing is like industrial  farm equipment for harvesting grunts  weapon unlocks are important and can  make some guns like the longbow DMR  sniper much more versatile but in order  to unlock the weapons themselves you  need to focus on XP and nothing delivers  big XP bonuses like pilot kills at the  beginning of a match run to where your  friendly grunts are clustered find  yourself a nice cloak position or wall  hang and then ambush the enemy pilots  that come a-calling if you can equip a  suppressor you can extend your ambush  longer by remaining hidden on the radar  if you score the first kill of the match  you'll get an XP bonus and because many  pilots use burn cards during their  initial deployment odds are you'll also  get an XP bonus for canceling set burn  card  speaking of which get in the habit of  using your burn cards you can only have  25 in your deck at a time and they fill  up quickly if you aren't using a few  each match use rare ones early on to  gain access to abilities your enemies  haven't unlocked yet like the active  radar pulse also known as the you neon  skeleton disco dance party  [Music]  now let's talk Titans if you're working  on your weapon attachment unlocks and  you want to stick to playing the pilot  don't let your Titan languish unbuilt  bring down your auto Titan and set it to  guard a slightly out-of-the-way area  it'll probably score some grunt kills  and off a pilot if you're lucky  alternatively set it to follow you then  listen for when it tells you that it's  engaging enemy pilots and Titans and  spring into action just don't do this  during close attrition matches as auto  Titans are pretty easy kills that will  boost your enemies attrition score  significantly and hinder your chances of  getting bonus xp for winning the match  if you can be one of the first to call  down your Titan in a match  perhaps by using burn cards be sure to  equip the chain gun the accuracy and  range makes it great for picking off  pilots who are moving quickly or perched  on rooftops it works well on grunts too  though stomping on the poor suckers is  just as effective and lets you stay on  the lookout for would-be rodeo riders  when you're playing as a pilot get in  the habit of taking potshots at Titans  that are in combat even if it's risky or  your priorities lie elsewhere you're  basically signing up for free assist XP  when that Titan gets doomed  also don't underestimate the  disorienting power of arc grenades  they're great for setting up a rodeo on  an enemy Titan infiltrating an enemy  occupied hard point or just ambushing  pilots who are unawares and finally if  you happen to pass one of these heavy  turrets on the map take a few seconds to  hack it to your side you'll get a neat  little XP bonus the hits it lands will  reduce your Titan build time and it'll  probably attract enemy pilots looking  for some quick XP who you can then  proceed to murder eyes check the  comments below for bonus tips and  strategies and add a few of your own and  happy Titan falling  [Music]
 

